---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
import GitHub from '../components/GitHub.astro';
import { github, download } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Your first words with Quill.">
  <header class="guide-nav shell"><a href="/" aria-label="Quill home"><Brand class="small-brand" /></a><GitHub /></header>
  <main id="main" class="guide section-shell"><h1>Your first words<br />with Quill.</h1><p class="guide-lead">From a download to a draft that sounds like you.</p>
    <section><h2>Make a little space.</h2><p><a href={download}>Download Quill for Mac</a>, open the DMG, and drag Quill into Applications. You’ll need macOS 26 or later.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Bring your words.</h2><p>Choose a folder for your notes. If you already use Obsidian, you can choose your vault. Quill reads your notes to create <code>Voice.md</code>, a guide to your writing style.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Choose a co-writer.</h2><p>Quill uses your existing sign-in for supported tools. Codex needs its CLI installed and signed in. Claude Code needs Node. Find the full setup list in the <a href={`${github}#co-writers`}>co-writer guide</a>.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Say the first change.</h2><p>Quill opens a practice email. Hold the right Option key, say “make it direct,” and release. You’ll see the new wording in the draft.</p><p>Keep it with <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>↩</kbd>, revert it with <kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>⌫</kbd>, or type a request with <kbd>⌘K</kbd>. Your words remain yours to choose.</p></section>
    <a class="text-link" href="/">Back to Quill <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </main>
</Base>
